    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a5166101-4cbc-5af0-b370-783b6a62bfc3",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x+y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nAssume $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}&=\\frac{x+y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}&={x}^{2}(\\frac{x+y}{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}&=x(x+y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}&={x}^{2}+x y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(- x)}_{P(x)}y&=\\underbrace{x^{2}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} - x y&=x^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=- x$ and $Q(x)=x^{2}.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "708f52e8-ffc1-5b6a-9ed9-3dea2242c590",
