      ":question/worked-solution": "A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 y^{2}-ye^{- x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}&=y \\\\ -ye^{- x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5 y^{2}-y&=0 \\\\ -y(e^{- x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5 y+1)&=0 \\\\ e^{- x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5 y+1&=0 \\\\ e^{x}(e^{- x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5 y+1)&=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5 y e^{x}+e^{x}&=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(- 5 e^{x})}_{P(x)}y&=\\underbrace{- e^{x}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} - 5 y e^{x}&=- e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=- 5 e^{x}$ and $Q(x)=- e^{x}.$",
